hls: a segment whose early open failed is asked for once more, without retries

With http_multiple, hls opens the next segment while the current one is
read. When that early open failed, its error was dropped: the segment was
requested again when it was due, with another round of http's retries, and
the failure did not start the live_reload_timeout of seg_skip=live. Further
early opens went on while segments failed, each holding up reading the
current one. A server that stopped answering thus held a live input for
several rounds of http's retries and timeouts.

Keep the error for that segment and count the failure from the start of
the early open. When the segment is due it is requested once more with
reconnect_max_retries 0: a short failure is over by then, while a server
that stopped answering holds the read for one more timeout rather than
another round of retries. A kept-alive connection keeps the options of its
last request, so every segment request now sets reconnect_max_retries,
to the caller's value except for that one. If the segment has left the
playlist by then, its failure still ends the playlist when segment
failures are final (seg_skip, live_reload_timeout). No early opens while
segments fail.

